{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_03adde549d86554f5a38331d79b1938234767068a65129b1b15e86f9b070e937","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b8c6e5100981c02b9ff08603ac35edffab12d4566ef374a3f4b49d234974ee72"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"The product works with local projects and remote machines over SSH, and drives CLI agents the user already has, such as Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and Amp.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0da47d90d37e39b1b0862666b0a0b9bb64201e01ffd1f8bd795344388a09cd27","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5cc40a89a0d52b271243491b95333ae154fd39b30f2ea9f2685465c04845cd27"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"Emdash automatically detects installed provider CLIs and supports agents including Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, OpenCode, Amp, Devin, Qwen Code, Droid, and GitHub Copilot.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_19fa31ca829cb9298196219c6f446d30c9136399ad70d71914fb43d3d128b84b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_25660d2334bc84a56b5c614dc67a6ad2f4c9a303ad90c13b93133fce55937138","slc_b215dad4d5d087702f54b8d5bf2c21353b8af447c3f491b56c37c82399f10835"],"source_ids":["src_543dca668cd857a484c06368309ca913"],"text":"Repository development practice: the merge gate is four root commands (format, lint, typecheck, test) run via pnpm/Nx, with CI running a code-consistency workflow using nx affected on touched projects and dependents, and browser Vitest projects skipped in CI.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3d4cd6a4a9c73b66fe5cf10bc74a617403e06e8f73625ff4489adb8b579ecd83","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c3e540c47c77a6c3bd90e7f221f2cd7447a3344be5f6e9a5bd8be69275a60188","slc_e864970326e41220d286fbc99937d5f394ce5252c8f5eb9ff41c8e0cc9a49844"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"Telemetry is optional and can be disabled in Settings or by launching with TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4d7dad5aa85c07803d0b404239d2d754bcdee89d2c16d5841cb68496915c99b7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_82ca6b09ce2749e9cdaead1b29ec581c43116b11b75af5ba67ce28637bebc766"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"The README notes that agent CLIs may send code, prompts, and context to their own providers, so data handling depends on which provider the user chooses.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6514d5b0d6701d5dd13283e71cfc97e125a884d14b6dc4257923ca12403de3fd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_aa481a4cfdff4c38e5237d1a5aabbdd676db3cf88ec70dddd4f1bb79b42147a6"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"Emdash is a desktop app for running AI coding agents in parallel, with each task isolated in its own Git worktree so multiple fixes or features can be explored, reviewed, and merged.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_77cfed20756f688336c7c0254efe2120271531ec035d1bd922fd196624f90964","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_972e4278b6180df27707738e53b22e1359ffa191e4e1e2aa51852b70c9df1ab8"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"Desktop builds are distributed for macOS (Homebrew cask plus Apple Silicon and Intel DMGs), Windows (MSI installer and portable exe), and Linux x64/ARM64 (AppImage, DEB, RPM).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7d08750c5326d617b80795b420eb2361d0355f7a86b6c6d3a94b02ad00f3fa23","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a8926eb39e481364c0b19031c772c5eb2f3f430ea8fd45dda1e02f1c857f7ec7"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"Features include running multiple agents without juggling terminals, per-agent worktree/branch isolation, sending issues from trackers like Linear, GitHub, Jira, and GitLab into agents, and reviewing diffs, creating PRs, inspecting CI checks, and merging from one place.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_805b85d9785cb040ac97653d33c1df42f89fd638524b1359c7aad5b0571cc28a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_07568e75fe24c7b882aae1e34b97e48c681edd849503f61ee05072a3870efb08"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"For agents with lifecycle-hook support, Emdash installs marker-tagged hook entries in the agent's user-level config to track status, notifications, and resumable sessions, and the hooks do nothing when the agent runs outside Emdash.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9e7fc5ac97f25d6e15cc3814748100478487b97578df8f9963da3ce9e2a55821","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0af8880646e011ad0c7119579a288d5b6bde3bb3e298676813d288f22b6bb869"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"Remote projects connect over SSH/SFTP with support for SSH agent, key, and password authentication, and credentials are stored in the OS keychain.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a21824de18d7b92dd3510f3c36b0a8a565f0de8bfb0cbd648456d3314f8fdede","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"generalaction/emdash@fccf35084709 snapshot a2795a7f46ba37a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_82ca6b09ce2749e9cdaead1b29ec581c43116b11b75af5ba67ce28637bebc766","slc_8379ac0dfe1d2a4d92811d97e324e192ef9745cbf3a7e1abdba03b1a93f5d7c7"],"source_ids":["src_5879b01558695dffbeacc4234d326bc9"],"text":"The app is local-first: app state lives in a local SQLite database, and Emdash does not send the user's code or chats to Emdash servers, though agent CLIs may send data to their own providers.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:50:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3fd4492ae6e6436ea7834c872c47bd7d"}
